<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4024.0">
  <POU Name="FB_Axis" Id="{fc68b3fd-d800-4883-a625-1424c3ae007b}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Axis
(*
    NC2 axis wrapper on Tc2_MC2: power, reset, three moves, a halt, a
    locking stop and a hold-to-run jog, with one status refresh and one
    error path.

    TEMPLATE - the moves, halt and reset were built and run on a
    simulated axis (4024.55); jog, Stop and the status properties have
    not been built or run yet. Test it on your axis at reduced velocity,
    acceleration and torque.

    CONTRACT
    - Call the body exactly once per cycle, unconditionally, before any
      code reads Axis.Status in that cycle: it calls Axis.ReadStatus().
    - The methods only record a request. The body issues it: on this
      scan's call if the method ran before the body, else on the next.
    - A method returns TRUE when the request was accepted, not when the
      axis has done it. bBusy / bDone / bError report that.
    - bDone, bCommandAborted and the command's error belong to the
      command eCommand names. A request that was accepted but replaced
      before it was issued (by Halt, Stop, Reset or a jog) still gets a
      result: eCommand names it and bCommandAborted is TRUE, until the
      next command takes over. A caller waiting for its own result
      checks that eCommand is still its command.
    - A stop wins: Halt and Stop replace a request still waiting to be
      issued, and while a Halt waits, moves, jog and Reset are refused.
    - Halt on an axis that is not ready (bReady FALSE: disabled or in
      error) returns TRUE and only ends a waiting move or halt. MC_Halt
      would be refused there with an error, turning an operator stop
      into an alarm, and the NC does not move a disabled axis anyway.
    - Stop is MC_Stop, the locking stop: from Stop() until ReleaseStop()
      the axis is stopped and held, and moves, jog and Reset are
      refused (bLocked). MC_Reset would release the lock. For an
      ordinary stop use Halt. Neither is a safety function.
    - Jog is hold-to-run on stMachine.bJogForward / bJogBackward, at the
      axis's manual velocities (slow, or fast with bJogFast). A button
      starts the axis only on its own rising edge; releasing it stops
      the axis. A press that is refused, or a jog that another command
      takes over, needs a new press: the axis never starts by itself.
    - Units are the axis's user units (mm, mm/s, mm/s^2 for an axis
      scaled in mm). Dynamics of 0 mean the axis parameters' defaults.
    - bBusy is about the command, not the axis. MC_MoveVelocity stays busy
      until something replaces it, and Tc2_MC2 ends it with CommandAborted
      when the override changes while the axis keeps moving. To know
      whether the axis moves, read Axis.Status.Moving / NotMoving, but
      not at override 0: with a move active there, NotMoving stays FALSE
      although the axis stands. Read the set velocity then.
    - MoveAbsolute is refused until the axis is homed: Axis.Status.Homed,
      or stMachine.bHomedOwn when the homed record is the caller's own
      (FB_HomePlc with bMarkNcHomed FALSE). One record per axis, not both.
    - stMachine.bLimitPosOk / bLimitNegOk go to MC_Power's feed enables,
      where hardware limit switches (NC contacts, TRUE = not at the
      limit) are wired. An open one stops that direction only.
    - The hardware enable of the drive is not MC_Power's; see the
      triage reference. No part of this block is a safety function.
    - Status is in properties, not outputs: fActPosition, fActVelocity,
      bHomed, bLocked, eCommand. They are copies made in the body, so
      read them after it.

    WHY TWO INSTANCES PER MOVE
    Tc2_MC2 takes no new parameters while a move block is busy. To
    retarget a running move, or change speed, a second instance of the
    same block takes over (BufferMode Aborting, the default); the first
    then reports CommandAborted, which here is expected and not passed on.

    WHY EXECUTE IS HELD UNTIL A RESULT
    Each instance's Execute stays TRUE from its trigger until it shows
    Done, Error or CommandAborted, then is FALSE for at least one call.
    An instance is triggered only when it is not Busy and was given
    Execute FALSE at its last call: every trigger is a real rising edge,
    and its inputs, which the block latches on that edge, are the ones
    the method recorded. MC_Stop is the exception: its Execute is held
    for as long as the stop is, because that is what holds the lock.
*)
VAR_INPUT
    bPowerOn  : BOOL;              // MC_Power software enable, both ways
    fOverride : LREAL := 100.0;    // velocity override, percent, 0..100
    stMachine : ST_AxisMachineIn;  // limit switches, homed record, jog
END_VAR
VAR_IN_OUT
    Axis      : AXIS_REF;          // the NC axis, linked in the I/O tree
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    bReady          : BOOL;  // MC_Power.Status: enabled and ready
    bBusy           : BOOL;  // a request waits or any command runs
    bDone           : BOOL;  // last command done; MoveVelocity: at speed
    bCommandAborted : BOOL;  // last command taken over by another block
    bError          : BOOL;  // axis, power or command error
    nErrorID        : UDINT; // NC code (scripts/nc_error.py) or cErr...
END_VAR
VAR
    fbPower     : MC_Power;
    fbReset     : MC_Reset;
    fbHalt      : MC_Halt;
    fbStop      : MC_Stop;
    fbJog       : MC_Jog;
    aMoveAbs    : ARRAY[0..1] OF MC_MoveAbsolute;
    aMoveRel    : ARRAY[0..1] OF MC_MoveRelative;
    aMoveVel    : ARRAY[0..1] OF MC_MoveVelocity;
    fbPendTimer : TON;
    fbStopEdge  : R_TRIG;
    fbJogFwdEdge : R_TRIG;
    fbJogBwdEdge : R_TRIG;

    // Execute of each block: TRUE from its trigger until its result
    bExecReset  : BOOL;
    bExecHalt   : BOOL;
    bExecStop   : BOOL;            // held while the stop is
    abExecAbs   : ARRAY[0..1] OF BOOL;
    abExecRel   : ARRAY[0..1] OF BOOL;
    abExecVel   : ARRAY[0..1] OF BOOL;
    nIdxAbs     : INT;             // instance used last, per move
    nIdxRel     : INT;
    nIdxVel     : INT;
    i           : INT;

    // the request a method recorded; the blocks latch it on their edge
    ePending    : E_AxisCmd := E_AxisCmd.None;
    fReqValue   : LREAL;           // position or distance
    fReqVelo    : LREAL;           // > 0
    eReqDir     : MC_Direction := MC_Direction.MC_Positive_Direction;
    fReqHaltDec : LREAL;
    fAcc        : LREAL;           // 0 = axis default; SetDynamics
    fDec        : LREAL;
    fJerk       : LREAL;

    bStopReq    : BOOL;            // from Stop() until ReleaseStop()
    fStopDec    : LREAL;
    bJogOk      : BOOL;            // a jog press may start now
    bJogFwd     : BOOL;            // MC_Jog's direction inputs
    bJogBwd     : BOOL;
    eJogMode    : E_JogMode := E_JogMode.MC_JOGMODE_STANDARD_SLOW;

    // Copied in the body: a method or property called from outside may
    // not read the VAR_IN_OUT Axis (compiler warning).
    bHomedNc    : BOOL;            // Axis.Status.Homed
    fActPos     : LREAL;           // Axis.NcToPlc.ActPos
    fActVelo    : LREAL;           // Axis.NcToPlc.ActVelo
    eCmd        : E_AxisCmd := E_AxisCmd.None;  // what results belong to
    bCmdError   : BOOL;            // its error, latched to the next one
    nCmdErrorID : UDINT;
END_VAR
VAR CONSTANT
    // Own codes sit above 16#FFFF, clear of every NC and ADS code.
    cErrNotIssued : UDINT := 16#0001_0001;  // request waited too long
    cPendTimeout  : TIME  := T#1S;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[// 1. Sensors first. Tc2_MC2 refreshes Axis.Status only when asked.
Axis.ReadStatus();
// Copies for the methods and properties, one scan old at most when they
// are called before the body, like bReady.
bHomedNc := Axis.Status.Homed;
fActPos  := Axis.NcToPlc.ActPos;
fActVelo := Axis.NcToPlc.ActVelo;

// 2. Stop and jog follow levels, so they start here, not in M_Issue.
//    MC_Stop runs only on a ready axis: on any other it would only raise
//    an error. It starts again when the axis becomes ready with the stop
//    still held. Its Execute rises only on a block that is not Busy (it
//    stays Busy some cycles after a release); once up, it is held.
bExecStop := bStopReq AND bReady AND (bExecStop OR NOT fbStop.Busy);
fbStopEdge(CLK := bExecStop);
IF fbStopEdge.Q THEN
    M_Start(eNew := E_AxisCmd.Stop);
END_IF

//    Jog starts on a button's own rising edge, on a ready axis that no
//    stop holds and no halt or reset waits for. Releasing the button,
//    pressing both, or any of those conditions ending, drops MC_Jog's
//    input, and MC_Jog stops the axis itself.
fbJogFwdEdge(CLK := stMachine.bJogForward);
fbJogBwdEdge(CLK := stMachine.bJogBackward);
bJogOk := bReady AND NOT bLocked
          AND (ePending <> E_AxisCmd.Halt)
          AND (ePending <> E_AxisCmd.Reset);
IF NOT bJogOk
   OR (stMachine.bJogForward AND stMachine.bJogBackward) THEN
    bJogFwd := FALSE;
    bJogBwd := FALSE;
ELSIF fbJogFwdEdge.Q OR fbJogBwdEdge.Q THEN
    bJogFwd := fbJogFwdEdge.Q;
    bJogBwd := fbJogBwdEdge.Q;
    M_Start(eNew := E_AxisCmd.Jog);   // a waiting move ends aborted
END_IF
bJogFwd := bJogFwd AND stMachine.bJogForward;
bJogBwd := bJogBwd AND stMachine.bJogBackward;
IF stMachine.bJogFast THEN
    eJogMode := E_JogMode.MC_JOGMODE_STANDARD_FAST;
ELSE
    eJogMode := E_JogMode.MC_JOGMODE_STANDARD_SLOW;
END_IF

// 3. Issue a recorded request once its block can see a real rising edge.
//    The timer runs after the attempt, so it only counts a request that
//    is still waiting, never one issued this scan.
IF ePending <> E_AxisCmd.None THEN
    M_Issue();
END_IF
fbPendTimer(IN := (ePending <> E_AxisCmd.None), PT := cPendTimeout);
IF fbPendTimer.Q THEN
    M_Accept();                 // the waiting request gets its own result
    bCmdError   := TRUE;
    nCmdErrorID := cErrNotIssued;
END_IF

// 4. Every block, every cycle, unconditionally. Only Execute changes.
fbPower(Axis := Axis,
        Enable := bPowerOn,
        Enable_Positive := bPowerOn AND stMachine.bLimitPosOk,
        Enable_Negative := bPowerOn AND stMachine.bLimitNegOk,
        Override := fOverride);
fbReset(Axis := Axis, Execute := bExecReset);
fbHalt(Axis := Axis, Execute := bExecHalt,
       Deceleration := fReqHaltDec, Jerk := fJerk);
fbStop(Axis := Axis, Execute := bExecStop,
       Deceleration := fStopDec, Jerk := fJerk);
// Standard modes take velocity and dynamics from the axis's manual
// motion parameters and ignore the block's inputs for them.
fbJog(Axis := Axis, JogForward := bJogFwd, JogBackwards := bJogBwd,
      Mode := eJogMode);
FOR i := 0 TO 1 DO
    aMoveAbs[i](Axis := Axis, Execute := abExecAbs[i],
                Position := fReqValue, Velocity := fReqVelo,
                Acceleration := fAcc, Deceleration := fDec, Jerk := fJerk);
    aMoveRel[i](Axis := Axis, Execute := abExecRel[i],
                Distance := fReqValue, Velocity := fReqVelo,
                Acceleration := fAcc, Deceleration := fDec, Jerk := fJerk);
    aMoveVel[i](Axis := Axis, Execute := abExecVel[i],
                Velocity := fReqVelo, Direction := eReqDir,
                Acceleration := fAcc, Deceleration := fDec, Jerk := fJerk);
END_FOR

// 5. Results. Drop Execute once a block shows its result, so its next
//    trigger is a rising edge; keep the result of the current command.
IF bExecReset AND (fbReset.Done OR fbReset.Error) THEN
    bExecReset := FALSE;
    IF eCmd = E_AxisCmd.Reset THEN
        M_Result(bOk := fbReset.Done, bAborted := FALSE,
                 bErr := fbReset.Error, nErr := fbReset.ErrorID);
    END_IF
END_IF
IF bExecHalt AND (fbHalt.Done OR fbHalt.Error OR fbHalt.CommandAborted)
THEN
    bExecHalt := FALSE;
    IF eCmd = E_AxisCmd.Halt THEN
        M_Result(bOk := fbHalt.Done, bAborted := fbHalt.CommandAborted,
                 bErr := fbHalt.Error, nErr := fbHalt.ErrorID);
    END_IF
END_IF
// Stop keeps Execute while it is held: Done is "stands, and locked".
IF eCmd = E_AxisCmd.Stop
   AND (fbStop.Done OR fbStop.Error OR fbStop.CommandAborted) THEN
    M_Result(bOk := fbStop.Done, bAborted := fbStop.CommandAborted,
             bErr := fbStop.Error, nErr := fbStop.ErrorID);
END_IF
// Jog is done once the button is released and the axis stands. A jog
// that ended otherwise needs a new press, so its input drops here.
IF eCmd = E_AxisCmd.Jog
   AND (fbJog.Done OR fbJog.Error OR fbJog.CommandAborted) THEN
    M_Result(bOk := fbJog.Done, bAborted := fbJog.CommandAborted,
             bErr := fbJog.Error, nErr := fbJog.ErrorID);
END_IF
IF fbJog.Error OR fbJog.CommandAborted THEN
    bJogFwd := FALSE;
    bJogBwd := FALSE;
END_IF
FOR i := 0 TO 1 DO
    IF abExecAbs[i] AND (aMoveAbs[i].Done OR aMoveAbs[i].Error
                         OR aMoveAbs[i].CommandAborted) THEN
        abExecAbs[i] := FALSE;
        IF eCmd = E_AxisCmd.MoveAbsolute AND i = nIdxAbs THEN
            M_Result(bOk := aMoveAbs[i].Done,
                     bAborted := aMoveAbs[i].CommandAborted,
                     bErr := aMoveAbs[i].Error,
                     nErr := aMoveAbs[i].ErrorID);
        END_IF
    END_IF
    IF abExecRel[i] AND (aMoveRel[i].Done OR aMoveRel[i].Error
                         OR aMoveRel[i].CommandAborted) THEN
        abExecRel[i] := FALSE;
        IF eCmd = E_AxisCmd.MoveRelative AND i = nIdxRel THEN
            M_Result(bOk := aMoveRel[i].Done,
                     bAborted := aMoveRel[i].CommandAborted,
                     bErr := aMoveRel[i].Error,
                     nErr := aMoveRel[i].ErrorID);
        END_IF
    END_IF
    // MC_MoveVelocity has no Done: InVelocity is "at speed", and the
    // command stays busy until another one replaces it.
    IF eCmd = E_AxisCmd.MoveVelocity AND i = nIdxVel
       AND aMoveVel[i].InVelocity THEN
        bDone := TRUE;
    END_IF
    IF abExecVel[i] AND (aMoveVel[i].Error
                         OR aMoveVel[i].CommandAborted) THEN
        abExecVel[i] := FALSE;
        IF eCmd = E_AxisCmd.MoveVelocity AND i = nIdxVel THEN
            M_Result(bOk := FALSE,
                     bAborted := aMoveVel[i].CommandAborted,
                     bErr := aMoveVel[i].Error,
                     nErr := aMoveVel[i].ErrorID);
        END_IF
    END_IF
END_FOR

// 6. Outputs. An axis error outranks the command's own error.
bReady := fbPower.Status;
// Busy while any instance still runs, not only the current one: a
// rejected retarget must not hide the previous move, which goes on.
bBusy := bExecReset OR bExecHalt OR (ePending <> E_AxisCmd.None)
         OR bExecStop OR fbStop.Busy
         OR bJogFwd OR bJogBwd OR fbJog.Busy;
FOR i := 0 TO 1 DO
    bBusy := bBusy OR abExecAbs[i] OR abExecRel[i] OR abExecVel[i];
END_FOR
bError := Axis.Status.Error OR bCmdError OR fbPower.Error;
IF Axis.Status.Error THEN
    nErrorID := Axis.Status.ErrorId;
ELSIF bCmdError THEN
    nErrorID := nCmdErrorID;
ELSIF fbPower.Error THEN
    nErrorID := fbPower.ErrorID;
ELSE
    nErrorID := 0;
END_IF
]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Method Name="MoveAbsolute" Id="{039bbf45-729e-4b81-a0e3-aa21e9af1d74}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD MoveAbsolute : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    fPosition : LREAL;    // target, user units
    fVelocity : LREAL;    // > 0, user units/s
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// Accepted while the axis is ready, no stop holds it and no halt waits.
// A velocity <= 0 is refused here: the block would reject it with an
// error while the previous move keeps running. Other bad values are
// reported by the block as an error.
// An absolute target needs a homed axis: refused until it is.
MoveAbsolute := bReady AND NOT bLocked
                AND (ePending <> E_AxisCmd.Halt)
                AND (fVelocity > 0.0)
                AND (bHomedNc OR stMachine.bHomedOwn);
IF MoveAbsolute THEN
    fReqValue := fPosition;
    fReqVelo  := fVelocity;
    ePending  := E_AxisCmd.MoveAbsolute;
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="MoveRelative" Id="{f714eace-0d29-4009-8cac-e4e7ec1bb981}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD MoveRelative : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    fDistance : LREAL;    // signed, user units
    fVelocity : LREAL;    // > 0, user units/s
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// Accepted while the axis is ready, no stop holds it and no halt waits.
MoveRelative := bReady AND NOT bLocked
                AND (ePending <> E_AxisCmd.Halt)
                AND (fVelocity > 0.0);
IF MoveRelative THEN
    fReqValue := fDistance;
    fReqVelo  := fVelocity;
    ePending  := E_AxisCmd.MoveRelative;
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="MoveVelocity" Id="{404b355c-5454-4476-b8b7-3e8749f29c72}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD MoveVelocity : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    fVelocity  : LREAL;          // > 0, user units/s
    eDirection : MC_Direction;   // MC_Positive_ or MC_Negative_Direction
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// Accepted while the axis is ready, no stop holds it and no halt waits.
// Calling it again while one runs changes the speed: the other instance
// takes over. The axis runs until Halt or another move.
MoveVelocity := bReady AND NOT bLocked
                AND (ePending <> E_AxisCmd.Halt)
                AND (fVelocity > 0.0);
IF MoveVelocity THEN
    fReqVelo := fVelocity;
    eReqDir  := eDirection;
    ePending := E_AxisCmd.MoveVelocity;
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Halt" Id="{bf6118a5-1b0d-4179-bbaf-1d77309bb738}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD Halt : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    fDeceleration : LREAL;   // > 0, user units/s^2; see the note below
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// Always accepted: a stop request is never refused. When the axis is not
// ready there is nothing to stop, and MC_Halt would only raise an error;
// while Stop holds it, it is stopped already. Then Halt only ends a
// waiting move or halt as aborted (a waiting Reset stays).
// MC_Halt, not MC_Stop: it does not lock the axis against the next move.
// Pass an explicit deceleration. For a value <= 0 the Tc2_MC2 manual
// says the last move's deceleration is used; not verified on a target.
// Only a Halt that is still the current command and still running is
// left to finish; a request waiting behind it is dropped, and eCommand
// stays Halt, the command that does run. In every other case a new Halt
// is recorded and replaces whatever waits, which ends aborted, and
// M_Issue triggers it as soon as the halt block is free again (an older
// halt being taken over by a move frees it within cycles).
IF NOT bReady OR bLocked THEN
    IF ePending <> E_AxisCmd.Reset THEN
        M_AbortWaiting();
    END_IF
ELSIF (eCmd = E_AxisCmd.Halt) AND (bExecHalt OR fbHalt.Busy) THEN
    ePending := E_AxisCmd.None;
ELSE
    M_AbortWaiting();
    fReqHaltDec := fDeceleration;
    ePending    := E_AxisCmd.Halt;
END_IF
Halt := TRUE;]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Stop" Id="{86f6fa68-2ee4-4ec4-a8a8-c0b0e0e0a2bf}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD Stop : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    fDeceleration : LREAL;   // > 0, user units/s^2; <= 0: last move's
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// The locking stop, MC_Stop. Always accepted. The stop is held until
// ReleaseStop: the axis ramps to a stand and stays locked, and moves,
// jog and Reset are refused meanwhile (bLocked). A new stop ends
// whatever still waits to be issued as aborted: a stop wins. Calling it
// again while held changes nothing, so it may be called every cycle
// from a held button: the running stop keeps its deceleration, and a
// Reset of an axis in error under the held stop is not undone.
// Use Halt for an ordinary stop; holding MC_Stop is the classic "the
// axis won't move again" bug. A software stop is not a safety stop.
IF NOT bStopReq THEN
    M_AbortWaiting();
    fStopDec := fDeceleration;
END_IF
bStopReq := TRUE;
Stop     := TRUE;]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ReleaseStop" Id="{3ab69ab5-5bf3-4f1e-a934-bbecefa4f838}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD ReleaseStop
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// Ends the hold: MC_Stop's Execute falls at the next call of the body.
// The block stays Busy, and the axis locked, for some cycles after
// that, so wait for bLocked FALSE before the next move or jog.
bStopReq := FALSE;]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Reset" Id="{e56054b0-7d6b-465a-90c6-1868a5623f01}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD Reset : BOOL
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// MC_Reset clears an axis error (and often the drive's). Refused while
// a stop waits to be issued, so a reset never swallows a Halt, and
// while MC_Stop holds the axis, because MC_Reset would release the lock.
// A Stop held on an axis in error is not running: Reset goes through,
// and MC_Stop locks the axis again once it is ready.
// While a reset already runs or waits, TRUE means "that reset covers
// it": no second one. A move still waiting is replaced, and ends
// aborted rather than vanishing.
// Find the cause first: resetting a repeating error hides it.
Reset := (ePending <> E_AxisCmd.Halt) AND NOT (bExecStop OR fbStop.Busy);
IF Reset AND NOT (bExecReset OR fbReset.Busy)
   AND (ePending <> E_AxisCmd.Reset) THEN
    M_AbortWaiting();
    ePending := E_AxisCmd.Reset;
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="SetDynamics" Id="{d886e02c-5e29-4f18-8e73-202a3db13d80}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD SetDynamics
VAR_INPUT
    fAcceleration : LREAL;   // >= 0, user units/s^2; 0 = axis default
    fDeceleration : LREAL;   // >= 0, user units/s^2; 0 = axis default
    fJerkValue    : LREAL;   // >= 0, user units/s^3; 0 = axis default
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// Applies to the moves issued from now on; a running move keeps the
// values it latched on its edge.
fAcc  := fAcceleration;
fDec  := fDeceleration;
fJerk := fJerkValue;]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="M_Issue" Id="{6e9c89d1-2bd5-46ce-a77e-6c6f9c318794}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE M_Issue
VAR
    k : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// Trigger the request on an instance that is free: not Busy, and given
// Execute FALSE at its last call, so the coming call is a rising edge.
// Dropping the flag is not enough on its own: a flag dropped after one
// call and set again before the next is TRUE at both calls - no edge.
// Not free: leave the request pending and try again next scan.
CASE ePending OF
    E_AxisCmd.Reset:
        IF NOT (bExecReset OR fbReset.Execute OR fbReset.Busy) THEN
            bExecReset := TRUE;
            M_Accept();
        END_IF

    E_AxisCmd.Halt:
        // Recorded while ready, but the axis dropped out or a stop holds
        // it since: see Halt.
        IF NOT bReady OR bLocked THEN
            M_AbortWaiting();
        ELSIF NOT (bExecHalt OR fbHalt.Execute OR fbHalt.Busy) THEN
            bExecHalt := TRUE;
            M_Accept();
        END_IF

    E_AxisCmd.MoveAbsolute:
        k := 1 - nIdxAbs;
        IF NOT (abExecAbs[k] OR aMoveAbs[k].Execute OR aMoveAbs[k].Busy)
        THEN
            nIdxAbs      := k;
            abExecAbs[k] := TRUE;
            M_Accept();
        END_IF

    E_AxisCmd.MoveRelative:
        k := 1 - nIdxRel;
        IF NOT (abExecRel[k] OR aMoveRel[k].Execute OR aMoveRel[k].Busy)
        THEN
            nIdxRel      := k;
            abExecRel[k] := TRUE;
            M_Accept();
        END_IF

    E_AxisCmd.MoveVelocity:
        k := 1 - nIdxVel;
        IF NOT (abExecVel[k] OR aMoveVel[k].Execute OR aMoveVel[k].Busy)
        THEN
            nIdxVel      := k;
            abExecVel[k] := TRUE;
            M_Accept();
        END_IF

ELSE
    // Stop and Jog never wait: they start in the body (M_Start).
    ePending := E_AxisCmd.None;
END_CASE]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="M_Accept" Id="{c756d66a-7cdf-45fc-9e06-af6d01ea63a2}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE M_Accept
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// The pending request becomes the command the results belong to; the
// previous command's result no longer applies.
eCmd            := ePending;
ePending        := E_AxisCmd.None;
bDone           := FALSE;
bCommandAborted := FALSE;
bCmdError       := FALSE;
nCmdErrorID     := 0;]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="M_AbortWaiting" Id="{316580ad-63cf-4239-be0b-de411cb13581}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE M_AbortWaiting
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// A request that was accepted (its method returned TRUE) but will not
// be issued still gets a result: it becomes the command eCommand names,
// ended with bCommandAborted. Its caller is never left waiting, nor
// reads the next command's result as its own.
IF ePending <> E_AxisCmd.None THEN
    M_Accept();
    bCommandAborted := TRUE;
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="M_Start" Id="{1d6525ee-416d-4333-a404-8166d26bd4ff}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE M_Start
VAR_INPUT
    eNew : E_AxisCmd;    // Stop or Jog
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// Stop and jog start in the body from a level, not from a request.
// Whatever still waits ends aborted; then eNew is the current command.
M_AbortWaiting();
ePending := eNew;
M_Accept();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="M_Result" Id="{fc1e80d4-31b8-4457-a451-822f1ad61d36}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE M_Result
VAR_INPUT
    bOk      : BOOL;     // Done
    bAborted : BOOL;     // CommandAborted
    bErr     : BOOL;     // Error
    nErr     : UDINT;    // ErrorID
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// Latched until the next command is accepted.
bDone           := bOk;
bCommandAborted := bAborted;
bCmdError       := bErr;
IF bErr THEN
    nCmdErrorID := nErr;
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Property Name="fActPosition" Id="{0d48a638-dd66-4aa1-ac1f-02abe27fe1b7}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY fActPosition : LREAL
]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{8ddd241f-ad26-48d9-8ea3-cdb993cbd308}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[// Actual position, user units: Axis.NcToPlc.ActPos.
fActPosition := fActPos;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="fActVelocity" Id="{7f6eccf1-1c9c-4e67-9c06-3b3f62969455}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY fActVelocity : LREAL
]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{970ec7a9-0a33-4127-b04a-1bb782fb891d}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[// Actual velocity, user units/s, signed: Axis.NcToPlc.ActVelo.
fActVelocity := fActVelo;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="bHomed" Id="{34fe1738-d2ef-4afc-9d4f-60939a66e397}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY bHomed : BOOL
]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{904f8192-d51a-4244-95f8-040ba8dcb5bf}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[// The homed state MoveAbsolute is gated on: the NC's Axis.Status.Homed,
// or the caller's own record in stMachine.bHomedOwn.
bHomed := bHomedNc OR stMachine.bHomedOwn;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="bLocked" Id="{c5c3ac28-f323-4f85-8f65-85afd1e303f9}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY bLocked : BOOL
]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{4dcc33af-5bc0-432c-a4e9-eb2b295ab01f}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[// Stop holds the axis, or its MC_Stop has not released it yet: moves,
// jog and Reset are refused.
bLocked := bStopReq OR fbStop.Busy;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="eCommand" Id="{b1146b60-91ad-42ee-88e7-5da549863dec}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[{attribute 'monitoring' := 'call'}
PROPERTY eCommand : E_AxisCmd
]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{87517a25-64cb-44a4-8a48-34aed36c0dae}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[// The command bDone, bCommandAborted and the command error belong to:
// the last one issued, or a waiting one that ended without being issued.
eCommand := eCmd;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>
